{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Clean</b>: Since all actions are done with the hands, he mentioned נקי כפים (clean hands) — that he did no evil. And it is בר לבב (pure of heart), which is the essence, and his נפש (soul) is the very glory of HaShem, as in: נשבע ה' בנפשו (HaShem swore by His soul)." "And it is written נפשי — by way of euphemism, on account of the glory of HaShem, in the manner of: והייתי אני ובני שלמה חטאים (then I and the children of Solomon would be offenders), as I explained. And so he mentioned deed, heart, and tongue."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:25.310647124Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}